    "slug": "what-is-an-ai-employee",
    "raw": "---\ntitle: \"What is an AI employee?\"\ndescription: \"Learn what an AI employee is, how it differs from a chatbot, and how Construct completes work across email, Slack, browser, and connected apps.\"\ndate: \"2026-07-02\"\nauthor: \"Construct Team\"\ntags: [\"ai-agent\", \"product\", \"ai-employee\"]\ndraft: false\n---\n\nMost AI assistants begin and end in a chat window. You ask a question, get an answer, and carry the result into the rest of your work. An **AI employee** goes further: it can accept an outcome, choose tools, complete a multi-step job, and preserve the files and context behind that work for later.\n\nConstruct is the work OS around that employee. It combines persistent files, inspectable memory, web research, a live browser, a sandbox terminal, a native inbox, schedules, workflows, and connected applications in one desktop.\n\n## Chat assistant vs AI employee\n\n| | Chat assistant | AI employee (Construct) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Workspace** | Primarily a conversation | Files, memory, tools, schedules, and workflows |\n| **Work style** | Answers or drafts | Executes browser, terminal, files, and apps |\n| **Continuity** | Depends on the current product and thread | Persistent workspace and correctable memory |\n| **Output** | Usually text in chat | Files, sent messages, app updates, and run history |\n\nThe difference is not intelligence alone. It is whether the agent has a durable place for work to live and the execution surfaces needed to finish it.\n\n## What Construct does day to day\n\nConstruct works from a purpose-built desktop with Chat, Files, Browser, Terminal, Email, Calendar, Workflows, Memories, Activity, and connected apps. You assign outcomes such as:\n\n- Research a market and save a cited report\n- Triage the agent inbox and draft replies\n- Update Linear issues from Slack messages\n- Run a recurring Monday morning competitor scan\n- Analyze an uploaded spreadsheet and attach a cleaned result\n- Build a small workspace app for a repeated internal process\n\nThe agent plans the steps, uses the browser, terminal, files, or one of more than 1,000 connected applications, and leaves the outputs in your workspace. Activity records show the actions taken and, when available, why a tool was used.\n\n## Work that persists and repeats\n\nPersistence makes an AI employee more useful than a one-off task runner. Construct keeps workspace files and long-term memory across conversations. Memories can be inspected, corrected, forgotten, or restored, so continuity does not require accepting an opaque record forever.\n\nSuccessful procedures can become reusable workflows. Construct workflows combine agent steps, connected-app actions, and notifications in a versioned linear run. Its native Calendar can run an agent task or workflow once, on demand, or on a recurring schedule.\n\nRead more about [AI workflow automation](/ai-workflow-automation) and [AI agent memory](/ai-agent-memory).\n\n## Work you can supervise\n\nAn AI employee should not become invisible simply because it works independently. Construct exposes files, browser activity, terminal output, workflows, memories, and Activity history in the same desktop. You can inspect results, interrupt a running turn, and answer questions when the agent needs missing information.\n\nConstruct can also delegate bounded subtasks to temporary agents. That helps with parallel research, analysis, implementation, and review while keeping the final synthesis with the primary agent.\n\n## When an AI employee makes sense\n\nChoose an AI employee when you need **recurring work**, **cross-app execution**, **persistent context**, or **inspectable outputs**. A chat assistant remains the simpler choice for quick drafting, brainstorming, and one-off questions that do not need tool execution.\n\nExplore the full [AI employee product guide](/ai-employee), read [Construct vs ChatGPT](/vs/chatgpt), or browse [all AI employee resources](/blog).\n"
